{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f48be5a19567f470","type":"text","text":"[[The Dawn Father, Pellor.canvas]]-> God of the Sun, battle and competition. the leading force in the ancient war between the gods during the calamity he was responsible for banishing and entrapping the God of hell Asmodeus in hell for all of eternity. His more notorious accomplishment was the killing of Tiamat turning her body into the prison he trapped Asmodeus in. His followers are one of many who aided in creating Vasselhiem.\n\n[[The Raven Queen, Matron of Ravens.canvas]]-> Goddess of death, fate, twilight and winter, a neutral God who hates and despises un death and immortality. She is although morally grey on the side of life will do anything to preserve it. She is known for being the only mortal to ever ascend to Godhood and her followers aided in building the most holy city in the world known as Vasselhiem. \n\n[[The Ever Light, Saren Rae.canvas]]-> Goddess of redemption, compassion, healing, temperance, and the dawn. Her followers are devoted to peace healing and prosperity. She is scarcely known for being the one of only two Gods during the calamity to kill a Betrayer God. However it is only known to her most trusted followers who that was. (It was The previous God of secrets Killaris). Her followers are the third and final group who rule over and created Vasselhiem. \n\n[[The Platinum Dragon, Bahamut.canvas]]-> Creator of the DragonBorn and God of justice, honor, and good-aligned dragons, He is notorious for his fight against Tiamant Who he killed and her body is now the Makings of the nine hells. His followers created the City known as Draconia where all dragon born live.\n\n[[The Wild Mother, Milora.canvas]]-> Goddess of nature and the creation of life. She was not very present in the war between Gods as her power is meant to preserve life and create it but never to take it. Unless absolutely necessary. Her followers are peaceful people mostly elven Druids inside of Vasselhiem and although they do not hold political power they are an essential part of the city's agriculture. \n\n[[The Knowing Mistress, Iuon.canvas]]-> Goddess of knowledge and Arcana. Her followers are very limited, mostly being Wizards and Sorcerers. Iuon is not a conscious being but is more like an ever present flow in all that exists in Villatoas, she sometimes comes to her followers but never in speech but in visions. In the war between Gods she sat idly by as her power is so vast the planet would not withstand her wrath.\n\n[[The Changebringer, Avandra.canvas]]-> Goddess of freedom, travel, adventure and luck. Mostly worshiped by traveling merchants and the occasional sell sword. Her role in the fight between Gods was to be a diplomat, known as a bit of a trickster and is the most often to appear to her followers. \n\n[[The All-Hammer, Moradin.canvas]]-> God of craft, creation, family and legacy. Most of his followers are dwarves. In the calamity he was known for creating all the weapons used by the Prime deities\n\n[[The Storm Lord, Normingander.canvas]]-> God of weather storms and lightning. Most of his followers are Goliaths. The body of the divine gate. Normingander sacrificed his body to create the Divine gate and separate Gods from the material plane.\n\n[[The Fairy Queen, Sylvine.canvas]]-> God of the Feywild and trickery. She does not have any followers and is very unknown by any people. She was one of the only Gods to nothing during the Calamity instead she hid away in the Feywild.\n","x":-300,"y":-160,"width":1480,"height":720},
		{"id":"20a2ef76181d7414","type":"text","text":"[[Gods.base]]\n#PrimeDeitie ","x":-300,"y":-320,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"14c7530e06e2bd26","type":"text","text":"Common Info\n\nThe Dawn Father, Pelor-> God of the Sun, battle and competition. The leading force in the ancient war between the gods.\n\nThe Raven Queen, Matron of Ravens-> Goddess of death, fate, twilight and winter, a neutral God who hates and despises un death and immortality.\n\nThe Ever Light, Saren Rae-> Goddess of redemption, compassion, healing, temperance, and the dawn. Her followers are devoted to peace healing and prosperity.\n\nThe Platinum Dragon, Bahamut-> Creator of the DragonBorn and God of justice, honor, and good-aligned dragons.\n\nThe Wild Mother, Milora-> Goddess of nature and the creation of life.\n\nThe Knowing Mistress, Iuon-> Goddess of knowledge and Arcana. Her followers are very limited, mostly being Wizards and Sorcerers.\n\nThe Changebringer, Avandra. Goddess of freedom, travel, adventure and luck. Mostly worshiped by traveling merchants and the occasional sell sword. \n\nThe All-Hammer, Moradin. God of craft, creation, family and legacy. Most of his followers are dwarves.\n\nThe Storm Lord, Normingander. God of weather storms and lightning. Most of his followers are Goliaths.","x":-378,"y":646,"width":1258,"height":494}
